{
  "id": "COMPOUND:43202 - PROTEIN:4968",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that 5H-Indolo[3,2-B]Quinolin-11(10H)-One may interact with ZR-75-1 through multiple pathways, with Ataxin-2 acting as a common target in two of the paths. In Path 1, 5H-Indolo[3,2-B]Quinolin-11(10H)-One is linked to Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which in turn is targeted by a compound that ultimately targets ZR-75-1. In Path 2, 5H-Indolo[3,2-B]Quinolin-11(10H)-One is directly linked to Ataxin-2, which is targeted by a complex compound that also targets ZR-75-1. Path 3 similarly links 5H-Indolo[3,2-B]Quinolin-11(10H)-One to Ataxin-2, which is targeted by 5-Oxobrucine, which in turn targets ZR-75-1. These findings suggest that the compound may exert its effects through a shared mechanism involving Ataxin-2, potentially through a downstream pathway that involves dehydrogenase/reductase activity or other enzymatic processes. The evidence supports a possible role for 5H-Indolo[3,2-B]Quinolin-11(10H)-One in modulating ZR-75-1 through a complex network of targets, with Ataxin-2 serving as a central node in this interaction.",
